# Resource Classification

Spec: Resources
Purpose:
  Define the resource taxonomy — what capabilities act upon.
  Resources have data classification levels that affect how
  context is assembled and presented to AI.

Owns: governance/resources.sdd

## Resource Types

### @resource.source-code
  type: codebase
  classification: INTERNAL
  description: Source code files in the project
  env_paths:
    local: ./src/**
    test: ./src/**
    staging: ./src/**
    production: ./src/**

### @resource.test-environment
  type: runtime
  classification: INTERNAL
  description: Test execution environment

### @resource.test-reports
  type: data
  classification: INTERNAL
  description: Test results and reports

### @resource.git-repo
  type: vcs
  classification: INTERNAL
  description: Git repository

### @resource.local-env
  type: deployment
  classification: INTERNAL
  description: Local development environment

### @resource.staging-env
  type: deployment
  classification: CONFIDENTIAL
  description: Staging environment

### @resource.production-env
  type: deployment
  classification: CONFIDENTIAL
  description: Production environment

### @resource.database
  type: data-store
  classification: CONFIDENTIAL
  description: Project databases

### @resource.internal-network
  type: network
  classification: INTERNAL
  description: Internal service-to-service communication

### @resource.external-network
  type: network
  classification: CONFIDENTIAL
  description: External network calls

### @resource.secrets
  type: credential
  classification: SECRET
  description: Secrets, tokens, passwords

### @resource.system-files
  type: filesystem
  classification: CONFIDENTIAL
  description: System-level files

### @resource.task-system
  type: management
  classification: INTERNAL
  description: Task management system

### @resource.skill-system
  type: management
  classification: INTERNAL
  description: Skill management system

### @resource.decision-system
  type: management
  classification: INTERNAL
  description: Decision management system

### @resource.model-files
  type: model
  classification: CONFIDENTIAL
  description: AI model weights and configuration files (HuggingFace cache, .safetensors)
  env_paths:
    local: ~/.cache/huggingface/**
    test: (n/a)
    staging: (n/a)
    production: (n/a)

## Data Classification Levels

  PUBLIC      — no sensitive data, safe for any context
  INTERNAL    — project-internal, safe for standard context
  CONFIDENTIAL— sensitive, redacted in review context
  SECRET      — highly sensitive, never loaded into AI context
  RESTRICTED  — must never access

## Classification Rules

  [RES-01] SECRET resources MUST NEVER be loaded into AI context as values.
  [RES-02] CONFIDENTIAL resources MAY be loaded as metadata only (reference paths, not values).
  [RES-03] AI MUST NOT attempt to read @resource.secrets directly.
  [RES-04] Runtime secret injection is the ONLY way secrets enter execution.

## Resource Context Loading

  Capability: code.read
    Resource: source-code
    Classification: INTERNAL
    → Full context OK

  Capability: db.read
    Resource: database (CONFIDENTIAL)
    → Context: schema, structure, not data values

  Capability: secret.access
    Resource: secrets (SECRET)
    → Context: reference exists, value NEVER loaded

